[2] Tournament Analysis
  vertices:
    proof carriers and observed packet states, not runners or arcs.
  pairwise observable:
    which carrier preserves the zero-regular-open LRC predicate while
    destroying the least boundary-owner/C27/K33/state-lift data.
  switch/gauge:
    majority over qdiv retention, Haar interior, boundary code, C27
    owner data, state-lift fit, and anti-scalar resistance; ties follow
    the printed Hamiltonian path.
  carrier scores:
    qdiv_gate                vector=(6, 5, 4, 3, 4, 6) note=strict q-witness before exact interval work
    Haar_open_front          vector=(5, 6, 5, 4, 4, 6) note=regular-open positive witness/discharge
    boundary_owner_skeleton  vector=(5, 5, 6, 5, 5, 6) note=zero-interior endpoint debt with owners
    C27_transfer_labels      vector=(4, 4, 5, 6, 5, 6) note=unit/nonunit shell ownership
    unital_affine_packet     vector=(4, 4, 4, 6, 6, 6) note=branch-local chart plus order/depth
    K33_state_lift_flag      vector=(3, 3, 4, 5, 6, 6) note=HYP-2908/THM-572 endpoint address
    wide_decorrelation_tail  vector=(3, 5, 3, 3, 4, 5) note=unbounded nonlocal escape control
    raw_runner_residue       vector=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1) note=too lossy alone
  hamiltonian_path=boundary_owner_skeleton > Haar_open_front > C27_transfer_labels > qdiv_gate > unital_affine_packet > K33_state_lift_flag > wide_decorrelation_tail > raw_runner_residue
